<title>BELGIUM: BRUSSELS BOURSE HALT - SAPEC .</title>
<headline>BRUSSELS BOURSE HALT - SAPEC .</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brussels bourse said in a statement on Monday trade in shares in Sapec on the double-fixing cash market had been halted for the day.</p>
<p>Shares in Sapec SA, a Belgian diversified holding company, closed at 1,510 francs on Thursday. Friday was a one-day market holiday in Belgium.</p>
<p>Belgian Cobepa holds 12.43 percent of Sapec. Group Financiere Frederic Jacobs and group Espirito Santo have 62.64 percent.</p>
<p>Sapec is one of the bidders for Portugese state chemicals company Quimigal of which 90 percent is to be sold this year, Portugese media have said. Sapec's bidding partner is chemicals group Mello.</p>
